Objective: https://carsalesdash-3tjwrwvv.manus.space/ (Live-Dash Board) 
Provide a clear overview of sales performance, trends, and business insights to help leadership make data-driven decisions.

Dataset Fields (assume typical structure):

* SaleDate
* Car_Model
* Brand
* SellingPrice
* Quantity
* Revenue
* Customer_ID
* Region / Province
* Dealer / Store
* Payment_Method

Dashboard Requirements:

1. KPI Section (Top Panel)

* Total Revenue
* Total Units Sold
* Average Selling Price
* Total Orders
* Month-over-Month Growth %

2. Sales Trends

* Line chart showing Revenue over time (monthly or daily)
* Highlight peak and low sales periods

3. Product Performance

* Bar chart of Top-Selling Car Models (by revenue or units)
* Brand performance comparison

4. Regional Performance

* Map or bar chart showing sales by Province/Region
* Identify best and worst-performing regions

5. Customer Insights

* Distribution of purchases (new vs repeat if available)
* Average spend per customer

6. Pricing Analysis

* Price range distribution (histogram or grouped bar)
* Relationship between price and quantity sold

7. Dealer Performance

* Top-performing dealerships
* Sales contribution per dealer

8. Filters / Slicers

* Date range
* Brand
* Car Model
* Region
* Dealer

9. Insights Panel

* Auto-generated key insights (e.g., “Sales peak in December”)
* Highlight anomalies or trends

Design Guidelines:

* Clean, modern layout (executive style)
* Use consistent color scheme (e.g., blue/grey business theme)
* Avoid clutter—focus on key visuals
* Use tooltips for deeper insights
* Ensure interactivity across all visuals

Output:

* Fully structured dashboard layout
* Suggested visual types for each section
* Clear labeling and titles
